sprdbt_tty on an SDIO WCN bus: the RX mbuf must fit MAX_PAC_SIZE

BT_RX_DMA_SIZE is the size of every RX mbuf that sprdbt_tty allocates and pushes to the
WCN bus. The realme source sets it to 2048, which is correct for the PCIe link it was
written for. On this board the WCN is attached over SDIO, where sdiohal derives the DMA
size from the mbuf length plus the 4-byte public header and refuses anything above
MAX_PAC_SIZE = SDIOHAL_BLK_SIZE * 2 = 840 * 2 = 1680:

    WCN SDIO: pac size > cp buf size,len 2052
    WCN SDIO: sdio adma write fail ret:-1
    Bluetooth: hci0: Frame reassembly failed (-84)

2052 = 2048 + 4, so every push of an RX buffer failed. The first failure also sets the
WCN carddump flag, and start_marlin() then refuses to power the BT function for the rest
of the boot:

    WCN SDIO: carddump flag set[1]
    bluetooth_set_power: end_block: 0, ret: -1
    mtty_open : set power failed , return!

1500 keeps the header inside the limit (1504 <= 1680) and is larger than any HCI ACL
packet the controller sends in one bus transaction.

Verified on the NX302J after this change: "pac size > cp buf" no longer appears in dmesg,
bluetooth_set_power returns 0, and mtty_open succeeds.

--- a/tty-pcie/tty.h
+++ b/tty-pcie/tty.h
@@ -34,7 +34,9 @@
 #define BT_RX_POOL_SIZE   1
 #define BT_SDIO_HEAD_LEN   0
 #define BT_RX_MAX_NUM 4
-#define BT_RX_DMA_SIZE 2048
+/* 2048 + 4 exceeds MAX_PAC_SIZE (840 * 2) on the SDIO bus; see this file's header. */
+#define BT_RX_DMA_SIZE 1500
 
 #endif